========================================================================
THE TREEBOLIC DECOMPOSITION: n = 2^{v2} * odd = (tree-depth, line-position)
========================================================================
  n  -> (v2=tree depth, odd=line position)   parity   note
   1 -> (v2=0, odd= 1)   ODD (tree top)   
   2 -> (v2=1, odd= 1)   even (depth 1)   pure power 2^1
   3 -> (v2=0, odd= 3)   ODD (tree top)   
   4 -> (v2=2, odd= 1)   even (depth 2)   pure power 2^2
   5 -> (v2=0, odd= 5)   ODD (tree top)   
   6 -> (v2=1, odd= 3)   even (depth 1)   DOUBLED PRIME 2*3
   7 -> (v2=0, odd= 7)   ODD (tree top)   
   8 -> (v2=3, odd= 1)   even (depth 3)   pure power 2^3
   9 -> (v2=0, odd= 9)   ODD (tree top)   
  10 -> (v2=1, odd= 5)   even (depth 1)   DOUBLED PRIME 2*5
  11 -> (v2=0, odd=11)   ODD (tree top)   
  12 -> (v2=2, odd= 3)   even (depth 2)   
  13 -> (v2=0, odd=13)   ODD (tree top)   
  14 -> (v2=1, odd= 7)   even (depth 1)   DOUBLED PRIME 2*7
  15 -> (v2=0, odd=15)   ODD (tree top)   
  16 -> (v2=4, odd= 1)   even (depth 4)   pure power 2^4
  17 -> (v2=0, odd=17)   ODD (tree top)   
  18 -> (v2=1, odd= 9)   even (depth 1)   
  19 -> (v2=0, odd=19)   ODD (tree top)   
  20 -> (v2=2, odd= 5)   even (depth 2)   

========================================================================
THE TWO RECURSIONS as the two directions of the geometry
========================================================================
  x2 (TREE DESCENT, clean vertical): (a,m)->(a+1,m)
       3 = (v2=0, odd=3)
       6 = (v2=1, odd=3)
      12 = (v2=2, odd=3)
      24 = (v2=3, odd=3)
      48 = (v2=4, odd=3)
  +2 (HOROCYCLIC, erratic in tree depth): weaves through levels
     2:(d1)  4:(d2)  6:(d1)  8:(d3)  10:(d1)  12:(d2)  14:(d1)  16:(d4)  18:(d1)  20:(d2)
     tree-depths visited by +2 from 2: [1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2, 1, 4, 1, 2] (ERRATIC = horocyclic)
  => x2 moves straight down ONE tree (clean); +2 is a horocycle weaving across
     tree levels. The two recursions = the two perpendicular directions of R x T_2.

========================================================================
PARITY DIVIDE = the 2-adic tree's FIRST branch; bridge x2 = descent
========================================================================
  odd numbers (v2=0) = the tree TOP (the 'odd line'); even = descended via x2.
  ODD = atomic/free (tree top); EVEN = doubled (one+ levels down). The bridge that
  carries an odd number n across the divide is x2: n -> 2n (down one level).

========================================================================
LRC TIE: channel cleanliness from (v2(n), odd(n)); the ADELIC interface
========================================================================
  n   (v2,odd)     n*=n/2^[even]   odd-part type        LRC channels
  13  (v2=0,odd=13)   n*=13          PRIME                CLEAN
  14  (v2=1,odd= 7)   n*= 7          PRIME                CLEAN
  15  (v2=0,odd=15)   n*=15          composite            filtered/messy
  16  (v2=4,odd= 1)   n*= 8          (unit, pure 2-power) filtered/messy
  17  (v2=0,odd=17)   n*=17          PRIME                CLEAN
  18  (v2=1,odd= 9)   n*= 9          prime-power 3^2      filtered/messy
  22  (v2=1,odd=11)   n*=11          PRIME                CLEAN
  => n=14=(v2=1,odd=7 PRIME) -> CLEAN (doubled prime); n=16=(v2=4,odd=1) pure 2-power,
     n=18=(v2=1,odd=9=3^2) prime-power -> filtered. The (v2, odd) treebolic coordinates
     of n predict its LRC channel structure. The ARCHIMEDEAN runner condition (||v t||
     >=1/n on R/Z) is obstructed by the p-ADIC channels (the trees) -- LRC is ADELIC.

========================================================================
WILD STRUCTURES (proposed): (1) BS(1,2) treebolic R x T_2 / Diestel-Leader DL(2,2)
(+ = horocycle, x2 = tree). (2) ADELES R x prod Q_p (+ at R, /p at the p-trees;
parity = Q_2's first branch). (3) the dyadic SOLENOID (inverse limit under x2).
(4) exp/log bridging + and x (primes = multiplicative frequencies). (5) WITT vectors
(+ and x unified via ghost components). (6) CAYLEY-DICKSON dim-doubling 1,2,4,8 (repo).
(7) STERN-BROCOT/Calkin-Wilf binary tree of Q+. WHY 2 is special: smallest prime AND
the archimedean place carries the SIGN (the order), so the +/x tension centers on 2.
